Java frameworks like Spring Boot are engineered from the ground up to handle massive concurrency and distributed systems, delivering superior sustained execution speed — a critical requirement for high-volume transaction processing and responsive agentic AI services.

The honest recommendation at 10k-agent scale is a **hybrid architecture**, not a single framework. Use LangGraph for orchestration/state, Spring AI for the execution layer's HA and concurrency, and ADK or CrewAI where their specific strengths apply (multimodal, rapid team expansion). The A2A and MCP protocols — all four frameworks support them as of 2026 — allow this hybrid without tight coupling, since agents from different frameworks can collaborate through standardized interfaces.

